At command is useful for scheduling one time tasks.
Example:-
=========

at time 

or 

echo "bash shellscript.sh" | at time

atq is used to display the pending jobs

atrm job_number is used to remove the job from the queue

at now+1 minute --> This command is used to set the execution of the command/script in the next minute.

at now+2 hours --> This command is used to set the execution of the command/script in the next 2 hours.

Crontab
-------

The crontab is used for running specific tasks on a regular interval.

syntax:- minutes hours days months weekdays command/script

0-59 --> Minutes

0-23 --> Hour

1-31 --> day

1-12 --> Month

0-6 --> Weekday

crontab -e to schedule a job

-l to list the jobs

-r to remove jobs


